WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:03.307
The team agreed on three
retries. Who remembers why?

00:05.150 --> 00:10.117
Briefnest brings the meeting, the email,
and the ticket into one Mac workspace.

00:11.100 --> 00:15.360
In sprint planning, Mira explains why
extra retries keep customers waiting.

00:15.500 --> 00:17.861
The approved notes give Asha the follow-up.

00:19.120 --> 00:21.840
Then an email confirms
the rollout for Friday.

00:23.040 --> 00:26.146
Bring in just the mailboxes
you choose for this project.

00:27.120 --> 00:31.920
Asha already has a ticket. Briefnest
checks Jira or Multica for existing work.

00:32.100 --> 00:34.368
A match can turn a new issue into a comment.

00:36.120 --> 00:38.274
Here’s the draft for the existing ticket.

00:40.070 --> 00:42.154
Edit it, dismiss it, or approve it.

00:43.130 --> 00:45.112
Later, ask why the limit changed.

00:46.760 --> 00:49.535
Follow the answer back
to Mira’s exact words.

00:51.100 --> 00:54.779
You choose which tools your AI
can read and what it can suggest.

00:56.030 --> 00:58.878
Briefnest. Where conversations
connect to the work.
